        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "UCE-4L shows an effect roughly an order of magnitude larger than the rank-encoding models (Geneformer V1, scGPT-human). One interpretation is that UCE's protein-embedding architecture preserves finer-grained transcriptional similarity than gene-token-based models, so contamination produces a larger geometric footprint. An alternative is that UCE's pretraining corpus (CELLxGENE Census, 36M cells) has a higher cell-by-cell overlap with our benchmarks than Genecorpus-30M; characterizing this would require an analogous Signal A audit against CELLxGENE Census directly, which we leave for future work.",
            "block_bbox": [
                124,
                1211,
                1065,
                1403
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
